# Laravel UI Integration – OpenCode Commands (WITH UI REFERENCE FOLDER)

## Task 0: Setup UI Reference Folder (READ-ONLY)

**Command:**

* Place your original UI folder inside Laravel project:

  /ui-reference/

* This folder contains:

  * .html files
  * .js files

**Rules:**

* DO NOT modify anything inside `/ui-reference/`
* Use it only as design reference
* All work must be done inside Laravel structure

---

## Task 1: Move UI into Laravel (FROM REFERENCE)

**Command:**

* Copy necessary parts FROM `/ui-reference/` INTO:

  * HTML → `resources/views/`
  * CSS → `resources/css/`
  * JS → `resources/js/`
  * Images → `public/images/`

* Do NOT copy everything blindly

* Only extract required sections

---

## Task 2: Create Main Layout

**Command:**
Create `resources/views/layouts/app.blade.php`:

* Extract layout structure from UI reference
* Add:

  * Head section
  * Tailwind + Vite assets
  * Navbar, sidebar, footer includes
  * `@yield('content')`

---

## Task 3: Create Partials

**Command:**
Create:

* `resources/views/partials/navbar.blade.php`
* `resources/views/partials/sidebar.blade.php`
* `resources/views/partials/footer.blade.php`

Copy corresponding sections FROM `/ui-reference/`

---

## Task 4: Convert HTML Pages to Blade

**Command:**
For each page in `/ui-reference/`:

* Create Blade version:

  * dashboard → `dashboard/index.blade.php`
  * bookings → `bookings/index.blade.php`

* Wrap with:
  @extends('layouts.app')

  @section('content')

  <!-- page content -->

  @endsection

---

## Task 5: Setup Routes (MANDATORY)

**Command:**
Edit `routes/web.php`:

Route::view('/', 'welcome');
Route::view('/dashboard', 'dashboard.index');
Route::view('/bookings', 'bookings.index');

---

## Task 6: Create Navigation Page

**Command:**
Create `resources/views/welcome.blade.php`:

<h1>UI Pages</h1>
<ul>
  <li><a href="/dashboard">Dashboard</a></li>
  <li><a href="/bookings">Bookings</a></li>
</ul>

